// LOOPBACK heartbeat for local single-box testing. Opt in with
//   -J../foam-saf/deployment/loopback
// when running two or more SAF instances on one machine, e.g.
//   deployment/<app>/run.sh -J../foam-saf/deployment/loopback
//
// Why: on the OS default interface a VPN (utun*) or an interface's reject route
// sends the 230.22.41.0 heartbeat group off the box, so instances on one machine
// never see each other's heartbeats -- healthDAO stays empty and SAF has no
// "destination is up" signal to forward on. LOOPBACK pins the heartbeat to the
// loopback interface instead.
//
// CSpec.service is a plain property, not an FObjectProperty, so journal replay
// REPLACES this block rather than deep-merging it onto the base
// healthHeartbeatService CSpec (foam3 foam/core/app/services.jrl). So
// multicastAddress and port must be restated here, kept in sync with the base;
// only `mode` is new. `enabled` is a separate CSpec property set by the saf
// deployment overlay, so replacing `service` leaves it untouched.
p({
  "class":"foam.core.boot.CSpec",
  "name":"healthHeartbeatService",
  "service":{
    "class":"foam.core.app.HealthHeartbeatService",
    "multicastAddress":"230.22.41.0",
    "port":52241,
    "mode":"LOOPBACK"
  }
})
